# Container safety

- Treat `/workspace` as the only project directory.
- Do not inspect host paths outside `/workspace`.
- Do not read secret files unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not modify `.env` files unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not run destructive commands without explicit approval.
- Do not run `docker system prune` or delete Docker volumes without approval.
- Do not start privileged containers.
- Do not mount `/`, `/home`, `/etc`, or other sensitive host paths.
- Treat `/var/run/docker.sock` as privileged access to the host.
- Explain commands that may delete, overwrite, or expose data.
- Keep new files owned by the current container user.

These rules guide the agent. They are not a security sandbox.
